Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:19:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Stop retrying an unscrollable partial display prefix

SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Chen Zhexuan
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

A multiline display prefix can leave the cursor row partially visible
even when the effective window start is already point. After the existing
forced-visibility phase, further buffer-position retries cannot reveal
that row without passing point. Return to the existing redisplay fallback
instead of repeatedly drawing the same prefix.

Keep ordinary conservative scrolling, the oversized-row acceptance phase,
post-scroll-hook start positions, and the top-vscroll exception unchanged.

--- a/src/xdisp.c
+++ b/src/xdisp.c
@@ -19739,6 +19739,13 @@
 		 (w, MATRIX_ROW (w->desired_matrix, w->cursor.vpos))))
 	{
 	  clear_glyph_matrix (w->desired_matrix);
+	  /* A multiline display string can put point below the first
+	     screen row even when the window starts at point.  Once the
+	     non-forced visibility test still fails, moving the buffer
+	     start cannot reveal more of that row without passing point.
+	     Let the fallback handle it instead of retrying forever.  */
+	  if (extra_scroll_margin_lines > 1 && CHARPOS (startp) == PT)
+	    return SCROLLING_FAILED;
 	  ++extra_scroll_margin_lines;
 	  goto too_near_end;
 	}
